   *
   * 2) Validate request body fields (only accept editable profile attributes: display name and phone number). If the request contains disallowed fields, reject as invalid request.
   *
   * 3) Ownership enforcement: ensure the resolved authenticated member id matches the profile record to update.
   *    - If the authenticated identity cannot be mapped to a valid profile record, return access denied / not found per existing conventions.
   *
   * 4) Perform the update as a single database transaction:
   *    - UPDATE shopping_mall_members with the provided editable values.
   *    - Update timestamps if they are part of the schema behavior.
   *
   * 5) Return the updated profile resource in the response model.
   *
   * 6) Edge cases:
   *    - If any validation fails, do not perform DB update.
   *    - If ownership validation fails, do not apply partial changes.
   *
   * Implementation detail note: although the requirements describe display name and phone number as profile attributes, this specification must map them to the actual member/profile columns present in the persisted schema. Use the real column mapping from shopping_mall_members and reject if the required columns are not present.
   * @nestia Generated by Nestia - https://github.com/samchon/nestia
   */
